Emerald 3DS changes to pret/pokeemerald 76463dac15cad36aca5e2b3f6366abf9e53f814f: Japanese number padding and the fields numbers fill
Applies after 0067-japanese-save-info.patch; apply with tools/bootstrap.py.

CHAR_SPACER (0x77), the international padding of right-aligned numbers and fields,
is a kana in the Japanese charset: the Japanese ROM pads with its space, so a
Japanese build makes CHAR_SPACER CHAR_SPACE (the genderless "symbol" strings of the
PokéNav, written as {UNK_SPACER}, become a space too). Its digits are 8 pixels wide,
where the international fields were sized for 6: the screens that cut numbers take
the Japanese ROM's layout of those fields. The summary's stats, Exp. Points (with
the word for "to go" that ROM shows, gText_EmptyString8) and move power and
accuracy; the party boxes' names, levels and HP, and their sprites; the Pokéblock
case's feel; the PokéNav ribbon list's lines; the battle's action and move menus
(that ROM's windows, text positions and cursors, the move type's label in its own
window). Other languages are unchanged.

